## New guard enforcement

The candidate module is byte-equal to the corrected host-tested copy
`77db50af0ff65dfa333b28584b48632c625d999984e7ff8fffd48cb0e52cdb0f`.
Only new helper/patcher copies changed. They now require the immutable complete
17-source supporting guard manifest and uniform LF/CRLF source bytes with
pinned normalized content. This binds full RX macro arithmetic, public getter
declarations, the SDK allocator dispatcher/free and zeroization, certificate
attach implementation, and actual HTTP→transport→ESP-TLS callback chain. Exact
classic ESP32 target and its positive target boolean are both checked. Every
guarded source is registered as a configure dependency; all three RX lifetime
sites still use the original audited SDK source. Installed SDK output paths are
rejected. The SDK commit/clean state must also hold before/after actual builds.

`prepare-checks.py` only imports the new patcher, validates current sources and
